@startuml TechSupply_Java_Package_Overview
!include ../_estilo.iuml
title TechSupply Solutions — Organización del código
left to right direction
package "erp-backend" {
  package "src/main/java/com/techsupply/erp_backend" {
    package "security" as Security
    package "maestros" as Masters
    package "compras" as Purchases
    package "inventario" as Inventory
    package "ventas" as Sales
    package "audit" as Audit
    package "notifications" as Notify
    package "common.api" as Common
  }
  package "src/main/resources" {
    artifact "application.yaml" as Settings
    artifact "db/migration\nMigraciones Flyway" as Migrations
  }
  package "src/test/java" {
    artifact "Pruebas de dominio\ny contratos" as UnitTests
    artifact "Pruebas HTTP e integración\nPostgreSQL / Testcontainers" as IntegrationTests
  }
}
Masters ..> Common
Purchases ..> Common
Inventory ..> Common
Sales ..> Common
Masters ..> Audit
Purchases ..> Audit
Inventory ..> Audit
Sales ..> Audit
Purchases ..> Inventory : recepción
Sales ..> Inventory : despacho
Security ..> Audit
Notify ..> Security : destinatario
UnitTests ..> Common
IntegrationTests ..> Migrations : esquema de prueba
IntegrationTests ..> Security
IntegrationTests ..> Masters
IntegrationTests ..> Purchases
IntegrationTests ..> Inventory
IntegrationTests ..> Sales
note bottom of Settings
  La configuración se proporciona por entorno.
  Las credenciales se mantienen fuera del repositorio.
end note
@enduml
